    "probe_text": "Here is every validation and side-effect applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`, in execution order. The chain is: `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` \u2192 `OwnerMapper.toOwner` \u2192 `ClinicServiceImpl.createOwner` (`@Transactional`) \u2192 repository/audit.\n\n## Validations (in order)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold `OWNER_ADMIN`, else **403**.\n\n2. **Request-body Bean Validation** (`@Valid @RequestBody`, runs before the controller body; any failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400**). The order *among* these constraints is not guaranteed \u2014 they're collected and reported together:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1,255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1,80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)`, `@TelephoneDigits` (must normalize to valid E.164 \u2014 8\u201315 digits, region-aware national length)\n   - `email`: `@Email`, `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `postcode`: `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n   - **Class-level `@ValidPostcodeForCity`** (cross-field): a 4-digit postcode must fall in the city's region range (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown city \u2192 any 4 digits). Violation reported on the `postcode` node.\n\n3. **Service-layer business validations** (inside `createOwner`, in this exact order):\n   - **a. Identity-collision check** (`rejectIdentityCollision`): look up owners by telephone; if any shares the full identity key (`telephone|email|householdId`) \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerException` \u2192 **409**.\n   - **c. City capacity**: `countByCity` (case-insensitive); if `>= 50` \u2192 `CityCapacityExceededException` \u2192 **409**.\n   - **e. Daily limit**: `countByRegistrationDate` (on the *adjusted* date); if `>= 100` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` \u2192 **429**.\n\n4. **Entity-level re-validation at persist** \u2014 on `save`, Hibernate re-checks entity constraints: `@NotEmpty` on firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone, and `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)` on telephone.\n\n## Side-effects (in order)\n\nBefore the service (in `OwnerMapper.toOwner`):\n- **Normalize into the entity**: `address` \u2192 `AddressNormalizer` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE); `telephone` \u2192 E.164; `email` \u2192 lower-cased. `id` and `pets` ignored. `sharesHousehold` read into a boolean flag (not persisted).\n\nInside `createOwner` (`@Transactional`), interleaved with the checks above:\n- **b.** `findHouseholdMembers` \u2014 query owners by last name (case-insensitive) with matching normalized address.\n- **d.** Resolve `registrationDate` (default = today if null), then apply `BusinessDayAdjuster.toBusinessDay` (weekend rolls forward to next Monday); **set on entity**.\n- **f.** Set `bulkSignupWarning = (ownersOnDate > 80)`.\n- **g.** Set `namesakeCount` = count of same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n- **h.** Set `householdSize = householdMembers.size() + 1`.\n- **i.** Set `customerCode = CustomerCodeGenerator.format(city, lastName, ownersInCity + 1)` \u2192 `\"<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>\"`.\n- **j.** If `sharesHousehold && householdMembers` non-empty: `joinHousehold` \u2014 compute a shared SHA-256-derived `householdId`, set it on the new owner, **and re-`save` each existing member whose householdId differs** (cross-row writes to other owners).\n- **k.** `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 INSERT; DB assigns identity id.\n- **l.** `ownerAuditLogger.ownerCreated(owner)` \u2014 writes an `AUDIT` log line (id, customerCode, registrationDate).\n- **Transaction commits.**\n\nAfter the service, back in the controller:\n- Build response via `toOwnerDto` (computes read-only projections: displayName, initials, membershipNumber, membershipLevel, locality, contactPreference, identityKey), set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return **201 Created**.\n\n## Notes\n- There is **no `@InitBinder`**, **no JPA `@PrePersist`/lifecycle callback**, and **no `ApplicationEvent` publishing** in this path. The only \"event\"-like side-effect is the audit log line; the only cross-row write is the household re-save in step (j).\n- `pets` has `cascade = ALL` but the mapper ignores it, so nothing cascades on create."
